A||||4||MooCow||Door bushing and pins??||||5||
Z||000000||MooCow||01-16-2001||11:55 PM||||There is a guy on Ebay selling the door bushings and the pins for a Fiero and are only $12.50 and another from the same guy is at $5.50.  Are these hard to install and do I have to take the door off to do it?  Any special tools needed?<P>                                Thanks Ken||||reg||5
Z||000001||bHooper||01-17-2001||07:02 AM||||take a look at Rodney's web site, under exterior.  he has door pins much cheaper!<P> <A HREF="http://www.rodneydickman.com/retail.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.rodneydickman.com/retail.html</A> <P>||||reg||2
Z||000002||FieroJoe||01-17-2001||09:34 AM||||You dont have to take the door off to do it, just have a helper hold the door while you are swapping the pins and bushings.<BR>  The hardest part for me was getting the damn spring back in to place, must have taken my dad and I a half hour just for that spring.<P>If you have a hammer and a steel punch, you should easily be able to hammer out the pins.<P>Also, with rodney dickman's pins, I had to grind them down about a 1/4" from the top because the were too long, but door is much stiffer now!<P>------------------<BR>FieroJoe<BR>c311t@yahoo.com<BR>AIM: Fiero87311, Snowboarder0311<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||william_thorniii||01-17-2001||10:24 AM||||Friends,<P>These items are not only available through our dear friend Rodney, but also most neighborhood auto parts stores.  Just look for a door hinge pin kit in the "HELP" section for GM 82 and up model years.  <P>They only cost around $4.  <P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||1
